<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Shizuku step 4B-2 (shizuku/README.md "4B-2"): build-type manifest overlay, used ONLY when :shizuku is part of the build.
    app/build.gradle.kts wires this file as the manifest of the `debug` and `release` source sets inside `if (shizukuIncluded)`. With the switch off it is not wired,
    so it is never read and the build is exactly as before. (The folder name `shizuku` matches no build type or flavor, so AGP never picks it up by itself.)

    WHY: :mika's library manifest declares  <provider android:name="rikka.shizuku.ShizukuProvider" android:authority="${applicationId}.shizuku" ...>.
    The built-in manager (:shizuku) declares  moe.shizuku.manager.ShizukuManagerProvider  with the SAME authority. Two providers with one authority = INSTALL_FAILED_CONFLICTING_PROVIDER.
    The manager's provider is a subclass of rikka.shizuku.ShizukuProvider that also answers sendUserService and calls disableAutomaticSuiInitialization(), and :mika only uses the
    class ShizukuProvider (no static ShizukuProvider.* call in its Kotlin), so Mika's own <provider> is removed and nothing is lost.

    HOW: a build type's manifest outranks src/main, and src/main outranks the libraries, so this marker is applied to the manifest that :mika contributes.
    The manifest merger keys a <provider> by android:name only; the authority below is repeated as documentation, it is not needed for the match.
    The marker cannot hit the manager's provider (a different android:name). With -PincludeMika=false and Shizuku on, it matches nothing.

    Do NOT move this element into app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml: it would remove Mika's provider in every build, including a :mika build without :shizuku, where that provider
    is the only thing that receives the binder from an external Shizuku app.
-->
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools">

    <application>
        <provider
            android:name="rikka.shizuku.ShizukuProvider"
            android:authority="${applicationId}.shizuku"
            tools:node="remove" />
    </application>

</manifest>
